Z*USER'S QUIDE: PRESS LEFT ARROW  OR "^ BEGIN" TO GLANCE OVER THE TEXT ** LINE FEED "=" CHANGES THE PAGE ** THE BRIGHTNESS IS CHANGED BY PRESSING "BRIGHT" ** THE DISPLAY IS TURNED OFF AFTER 30S AND TURNS ON BY PRESSING ANY KEY ** þZ** SETTINGS: FIXED SETTINGS ARE USED BY PRESSING "^ CONF" ** TO CLANCE OVER SETTINGS PRESS "CONF" AND "=" IF NO CHANGES ARE NEEDED PRESS "=" AND THE NEXT SETTING IS DISPLAYED  ** CHANGING THE SETTING: PRIVATE ADDRESS; WRITE ON ** GRPOUP ADDRESES; WRITE ON, PRESS "=" ** ( "DEL" CORRECTS THE PRECEDING CHARACTER) ** DAY'S KEY/FIXED KEY; CHOOSE BY "DELETE" ** NOT AUTOACK/AUTOACK; AS BEFORE ** SOUND ALARM OFF/ON; AS BEFORE ** XMT SPEED; AS BEFORE ** LOW/HIGH OUTPUT LEVEL; AS BEFORE ** PRINTER:/RCV/XMT/XMT+RCV/RCV(DEL)/XMT + RCV(DEL)/NOT IN USE; AS BEFORE ** PRTR-I: SPEED, PARITY; SPEED AS BEFORE, PARITY BY "P", TELEX MODE BY "T" ** COMP-I: AS PRTR-I ** þZ** (KEY, CLOCK, DELETE): FOR CHECKING THE KEY WORD PRESS "KEY" ** THE NEW KEY: PRESS "^ KEY" AND FINALLY "=" ** TIME: PRESS "^ TIME ** THE ENTIRE CONTENTS OF THE MEMORY IS DELETED BY KEYING "^T" AND "^K" ** þZ** EDITING AND CHANGING THE TEXT: PRESS "0" TO EDIT THE TEXT ** "DEL" DELETES THE CHARACTER PRECEDING THE CURSOR ** ARROWS TO LEFT AND RIGTH MOVE THE TEXT. (WHEN PRESSING CONTINUOSLY A WORD AT A TIME) ** "^ BEGIN" DISPLAYS THE TOP AND "^ END" THE BOTTOM OF THE TEXT ** "^ DELETE" DELETES THE MSG ** FIXED FORMAT MSG: THE SEQUENCE IS INITIATED BY PRESSING ONE OF THE KEYS FROM 1 TO 9 OR FROM ^0 TO ^9 ** þZ** TRANSMITTING THE MSG: NORMALLY THE LONG MSG IS TRANSMITTED. PRESS "^ SHORT" IF THE SHORT TRANSMITTING BUFFER IS WANTED. IF A RECEIVED MSG IS BEING DISPLAYED, IT CAN BE TRANSMITTED. WHEN PRESSING "SEND" AND "=" THE MSG IS TRANSMITTED TO THE RECEIVER:XX . IF IT IS NOT THE DESIRED ONE, TYPE IN THE NEW ADDRESS BEFORE PRESSING "=". THE XMT LED INDICATES WHEN THE TRANSMITTING IS ON. WHEN THE MSG HAS BEEN TRANSMITTED "SEND" IS DISPLAYED AND IF IT IS ACKNOWLEDGED "ACK" IS DISPLAYED. KEYS "ACK" AND "NAK" ARE USED WHEN THE MSG IS ACKNOWLEDGED OR NOT **þZ** RECEIVING AND READING THE MSG: RECEIVING LED INDICATES THAT THERE IS A MSG IN THE MEMORY, WHICH YOU HAVEN'T SEEN. IF "RECEIVING MEMORY FULLL" IS DISPLAYED DELETE THE MSG:S YOU DON'T NEED ANY MORE. BY PRESSING "DISPL" A PROMPT "MESSAGE 1...N?" WILL BE DISPLAYED. BY KEYING IN A NUMBER FROM 1 TO N THE RESPECTIVE MSG WILL BE DISPLAYED ** IF "DE" IS DISPLAYED IT MEANS DATA ERROR AND "CE" CLOCK ERROR ** TO SEE THE ENTIRE MSG PRESS THE ARROW TO LEFT. NOW YOU CAN CLANCE OVER THE MSG BY USING THE ARROWS ** "DISPL" DISPLAYS THE NEXT MSG ** "^ DELETE" DELETES THE MSG AND DISPLAYS THE NEXT ** ANY MSG BEING DISPLAYED CAN BE PRINT OUT BY KEYING "PRINT" ** þZ** THE MSG ENCRYPTION: THE MSG BEING DISPLAYED IS ENCRYPTED BY PRESSING "^ ENCR". THE ENCRYPTED MSG IS CONSTITUTED OF GROUPS OF FIVE LETTERS ** IF WANTED, TWO GROUPS ARE ALWAYS DISPLAYED UPON PRESSING THE ARROW TO THE LEFT ** THE RECEIVED (OR EDITED) AND ENCRYPTED MSG IS DECRYPTED BY KEYING "DECR". USE THE ARROW KEY UNTIL THE ENTIRE MSG HAS BEEN DECRYPTED ** þZ** CHARGING: THE EXTERNAL POWER SOURCE OF 10...30V/DC IS USED FOR CHARGING THE ACCUMULATORS. THREE DIFFERENT CHARGING MODES ARE AVAILABLE: 1. CHARGING, 2. QUICK CHARGING, 3. FAST CHARGING ** SEQUENCE: PRESS THE "^C". THE DESIRED MODE OF CHARGING IS DEFINED BY ANSWERING YES OR NO TO THE ALTERNATIVES DISPLAYED ** þÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿ